    <!-- Solar System Info Modal -->
    <div class="solar-info-modal" id="solar-info-modal">
      <div class="solar-info-modal-content">
        <button class="solar-info-close">&times;</button>
        <h2>How the Solar System Works</h2>
        <div class="solar-info-body">
          <h3>Overview</h3>
          <p>This interactive 3D solar system is built using <strong>Three.js</strong>, a powerful JavaScript library for 3D graphics. The entire scene is rendered in real-time on an HTML5 canvas element.</p>
          
          <h3>Key Components</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Scene & Camera:</strong> A 3D scene contains all objects, and a perspective camera provides the view. The camera can be rotated and zoomed using mouse/touch controls.</li>
            <li><strong>The Sun:</strong> A bright yellow sphere with multiple glow layers and a point light source that illuminates the entire system.</li>
            <li><strong>Planets:</strong> Eight planets orbit the sun at different distances and speeds. Each planet has unique colors, sizes, and rotation speeds.</li>
            <li><strong>Moons:</strong> Some planets have moons that orbit around them, creating a nested orbital system.</li>
            <li><strong>Asteroid Belt:</strong> 200 asteroids form a belt between Mars and Jupiter, each rotating independently.</li>
            <li><strong>Stars Background:</strong> 30,000 star particles create a deep space backdrop.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Interactivity</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Drag to Rotate:</strong> Click and drag to rotate the camera around the solar system</li>
            <li><strong>Scroll to Zoom:</strong> Use mouse wheel or pinch to zoom in/out</li>
            <li><strong>Auto-Orbit:</strong> When idle, the camera automatically orbits around the system</li>
            <li><strong>Click Planets:</strong> Click on planets to see their information (coming soon)</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Technical Details</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Animation Loop:</strong> Uses <code>requestAnimationFrame</code> for smooth 60fps rendering</li>
            <li><strong>Orbital Mechanics:</strong> Planets move using circular orbital math: <code>x = cos(angle) * distance</code></li>
            <li><strong>Materials:</strong> Uses gradient materials for realistic planet surfaces and atmospheric effects</li>
            <li><strong>Lighting:</strong> Multiple light sources (ambient, directional, point) create depth and realism</li>
            <li><strong>Performance:</strong> Optimized with efficient geometry and material reuse</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Code Structure</h3>
          <pre><code>// Main components:
- initGlobe() - Initializes Three.js scene
- Planet creation loop - Generates all planets with properties
- Animation loop - Updates positions every frame
- Camera controls - Handles user interaction
- Event listeners - Mouse, touch, and wheel events</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="solar-info-overlay"></div>
    </div>

